{"text": "Science is the study of things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That can be observed or measured in our material reality. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> We have built the modern world. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> On a set of processes that we call the scientific method. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That advance our understanding of the nature of that reality. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Metaphysics, on the other hand. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Is the study of the things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That lie outside of that material reality. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Such as the nature of the mind, consciousness, being, causality. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And, well, pretty much everything we wonder about. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But do not have a scientific way to investigate. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The line between the two is fuzzy. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And it shifts. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As science solves old mysteries. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And uncovers new ones. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But it would be a mistake. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To say that scientific truths. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Are the only ones we can ever know for certain. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Rather, they are the only ones we can prove. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> , a very different thing. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In point of fact. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The vast majority of what you know. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cannot be scientifically proven. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The old reporters adage. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If your mother says she loves you. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Check it out. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Is funny. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Because you cannot check it out. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But you can obviously know it to be true.", "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "c", "i", "e", "n", "c", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "u", "d", "y", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\